/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/comments.md:56:Use the `--comments` (`-c`) argument to include your comments as actions. If you do, do not add a `*` to the front of a line in multiline comments; it will make its way into the Shortcut.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/comments.md:60:You can use the comment action to explicitly add a comment action without including your slash syntax comments.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:2:title: Actions
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:9:# Actions
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:11:Actions in Cherri are intended to be easier to use, as in some cases, single actions have been split up into multiple
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:12:actions to reduce the number of arguments and complexity. Some arguments are optional, and some are required.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:14:Actions can be used just like you would call a function in another language
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:20:## Standard Actions
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:22:Below are categories of standard Shortcut actions currently supported. Keep in mind that actions in each category, other than the basic actions, need to be included.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:24:[Please report incomplete or non-working actions](https://github.com/electrikmilk/cherri/issues)
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:26:## Can I contribute actions, even non-standard actions?
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/actions.md:30:[Learn more about contributing actions]({{ '/compiler/actions' | relative_url }})
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/references.md:13:Some Shortcut actions accept files or media items that are bound to a specific device — for example, a specific file in iCloud Drive or a song in your Music library. These values cannot be written by hand; they must be captured from a Shortcut that already has them configured.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/references.md:27:Open the Shortcuts app on your Apple device and add the file or media argument to the relevant action in your Shortcut. This is required because only the Shortcuts app can resolve and embed the device-specific identifiers for these values.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/references.md:56:## Using references in actions
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/references.md:58:Pass the reference identifier as an argument to any action that accepts it:
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/references.md:83:| `identifier` | Name used to refer to this value in action arguments. Derived from the file or media item name when extracted. Feel free to change it, just be sure to also rename usages of it. |
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:2:title: Action Definitions
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:8:# Action Definitions
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:19:To define a Shortcut action raw, in the same reusable way as the [standard Shortcut actions]({{ '/language/actions' | relative_url }}) in the compiler, use the following syntax:
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:22:action 'com.example.app.action' myCustomAction()
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:24:myCustomAction()
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:27:A raw text `WFWorkflowActionIdentifier` is required between `action` and the identifier of the action.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:29:The only exception to this is for Shortcuts actions that start with `is.workflow.actions`. If the identifier namespaces are less than 4, we assume it is a classic Shortcuts action for the convenience of defining them.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:31:You may see `#builtin` for an action definition printed by the compiler. These actions are internally defined in the compiler and require compile-time processing that either cannot practically be abstracted to Cherri or hasn't yet been implemented.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:35:To find the identifier and parameters for an action from a Shortcut not implemented in Cherri, see [parsing out action data from a raw Shortcut]({{ '/faq#how-do-i-use-non-standard-actions' | relative_url }}).
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:39:Attributes may be added in the following order after `action`:
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:41:- `default` - For decompilation, if multiple action definitions use the same identifier, use this action by default if no other actions match better.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:42:- `mac`: - macOS-only action _OR_ `!mac`: non macOS action, iOS/iPadOS only.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:47:The syntax for the action arguments is the same as [functions]({{ '/language/functions#defining-arguments' | relative_url }}), and you can also set an [output type]({{ '/language/custom-actions#output-type' | relative_url }}).
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:52:action 'com.example.app.action' myCustomAction(variable file: 'WFInput'): bool
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:55:myCustomAction(@file)
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:60:To add extra parameters in the same way as a [raw action]({{ '/language/raw-actions' | relative_url }}), add a dictionary after the definition and an optional output type.
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:63:action 'com.example.app.action' myCustomAction(variable file: 'WFInput'): bool {
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:64:    "WFActionParameterName": true
/home/runner/work/cherri/cherri/cherrilang.org/language/action-definitions.md:70:Below is an example using the **Show Alert** action.
